      "id": 1,
      "text": "Paseo was built in 1929 as the first commercial shopping district north of Downtown Oklahoma City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paseo_Arts_District",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The district’s Spanish‑revival architecture remains intact, with stucco buildings and clay‑tile roofs that give it a village feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.travelok.com/paseo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Since 1975, Paseo has hosted an annual arts festival each Memorial Day weekend, showcasing original visual and performing works.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paseo_Arts_District",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The First Friday Gallery Walk, held every month, invites visitors to art openings, wine tastings, and live music in the galleries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.travelok.com/paseo",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Paseo Arts Association, formally organized in the 1970s, sparked the revitalization that turned the area into a creative hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thepaseo.org/history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The former Anglican church, moved from New Brunswick in 2000, now serves as a venue for weddings and events in the district.",
